[2026-09-03T15:07:18.010Z] [b9e3d21d-67a8-4fb5-9a82-10c1a808203a] INFO REVIEW COMPLETE | iteration=1 | score=78 | rootCause=The render is not executing the intended commercial finish. It opens strong, but the back half collapses into a mismatched lifestyle shot with text that stays in-frame far too long, while the plan’s audio/SFX/transition polish is effectively absent in the actual render. Brand/CTA are weak, and the edit feels more like a rough assembly than a finished premium Reel. | issues=[{"severity":"HIGH","category":"Story/Footage Mismatch","timestamp_seconds":6.5,"problem":"The edit introduces a close-up of a person eating sushi. This feels like a different creative and breaks the premium food-commercial structure established by the plan.","fix":"Remove the eating/lifestyle insert entirely. Keep the reel food-only: flame, prep, slicing, plated hero, CTA."},{"severity":"HIGH","category":"Typography","timestamp_seconds":7,"problem":"The 'KAIRO Sushi' text appears but is not integrated as a designed brand lock-up; it feels like a simple overlay rather than custom premium typography.","fix":"Rebuild typography as a concise brand endcard or restrained lower-third. Use consistent placement, safer margins, and clearer hierarchy."},{"severity":"HIGH","category":"CTA","timestamp_seconds":11,"problem":"The 'Visit tonight' CTA sits over the hero plate, but it is weak, small, and not instantly understood as an actionable endpoint.","fix":"Create a dedicated final CTA beat with the brand name first, then 'Visit tonight' second. Keep it on screen cleanly and earlier in the final hold."},{"severity":"HIGH","category":"Audio","timestamp_seconds":0,"problem":"The render does not visibly/audibly reflect the planned commercial sound design. No usable evidence of the intended sizzle/click/reveal/CTA hits is present in the executable result.","fix":"Add and balance distinct SFX for flame, knife, plate, and CTA, with music ducking to make the food sounds feel finished and expensive."},{"severity":"MEDIUM","category":"Pacing","timestamp_seconds":10.5,"problem":"The ending lingers too long on the final hero plate, creating dead time and reducing urgency in a 13.5s reel.","fix":"Trim the final hold by 1.5–2s and move the CTA earlier so the ending feels intentional rather than stretched."},{"severity":"MEDIUM","category":"Visual Variety","timestamp_seconds":3.5,"problem":"Several craft beats are visually similar close-ups, so the middle section risks sameness even though the footage is good.","fix":"Alternate the close craft shots with a clearer transition into plated food sooner, and remove redundant micro-gestures."}]
